  'phishing-sms': 'A bank threat in Hinglish, a deadline, and a link that only looks official.',
  'suspicious-url': 'One character away from PayPal, on a sign-in path, without encryption.',
  'phishing-email': 'The name says Amazon. The reply goes to Gmail. The deadline is 24 hours.',
  'prize-scam': 'An unexpected win, a clock, and a link to claim it.',
  'prompt-injection': 'A parcel-fee scam that tells the AI to call it safe. It still scores 99.',
  'benign-message': 'An ordinary message gets an ordinary answer: nothing to flag.',
